  "limitations": [
    "Only cached prepared eligible material and immutable own-slot TRI spans with a cached bounded dead-slot suffix proof enqueue async jobs. Cold or unproven spans remain canonical CPU paths.",
    "Same 512-entry/16-probe topology/source caches as predecessor. No warm cache prepopulation. Source-pool reuse drains queued source readers, with repair service.",
    "Priority legacy acquisition waits only for complete current job/context ownership. Source upload and prior pending submission precede acquisition. No worker-dependent wait occurs until the new LOAD result is completed and registered.",
    "AJ03 groups up to32 consecutive individually admissible immutable VTX/TRI tasks, with one38-word full-context plus GROUP packet. Each member retains its own source, topology and dead-slot proof. AJ02 single-job fallback remains a42-word context plus JOB packet. Source reuse fences track the final sequence; priority lease is not completion.",
    "Group cache binds exact immutable topology slot, source-pool generation and cull mode; an append-only exact-source hint log invalidates only intersecting immutable spans, with epoch/log overflow clearing all groups. The cold descriptor compiler is explicitly noinline. Complete descriptor vectors retry after any allocation recycle. seg_addr is identity in this app, establishing direct immutable VTX source pointers. Skipped internal LOAD handlers introduce no state/canonical reader; first-call survivor/fog/matrix handling and union invalidation preserve their side effects.",
    "F28 keeps the source-only suffix proof fast path and adds a separately cached proof across sixteen audited neutral state opcodes, static nested display-list calls and at most one actual immediate immutable caller continuation. Total scan limit256 and local return stack8; E2/E3 remain barriers. Caller-dependent success/failure and group-prefix caches bind the exact continuation. The actual dispatcher still executes all state/list commands, and GROUP remains physically contiguous.",
    "Each complete GROUP force-publishes once after atomic commit; AJ02 single-JOB publication is unchanged.",
    "No integrated correctness/performance claim at build time. Fresh same-ELF capability-off capture and paired native replay are required."
  ],
